@startuml save-to-fhir-components
!theme plain
title Components and how a composition becomes a displayed Patient Summary

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam nodesep 45

package "nictiz-ui" {
  component "**openEHR UI**\ncomposition form" as FORM
  component "**FHIR UI**\npatient summary viewer" as SUM
  FORM ..> SUM : **5.** hand over\nthe Bundle id
}

database "**openEHR CDR**\nEHRbase" as EHR
component "**openFHIR**\nFHIR Connect\nmapping engine" as OF
database "**FHIR server**\nHAPI" as HAPI

FORM --> EHR  : **1.** store composition\n**2.** read back (canonical)
FORM --> OF   : **3.** translate to FHIR
FORM --> HAPI : **4.** store Bundle
SUM  --> HAPI : **6.** fetch Bundle by id

OF ..> EHR : reads the\ntemplate (OPT)

note as N1
  Both UIs reach the three services through a thin
  backend-for-frontend: nothing in the stack allows
  CORS, and the CDR credential must not reach the browser.
end note

note as N2
  Steps 3-6 are **non-fatal**. The composition is already
  committed by then, so a failed translation leaves the
  record intact — only the summary is unavailable.
end note

FORM .. N1
OF .. N2

@enduml
